## Back-End — Code quality

When changing **tradeup-api** PHP (non-test) code, follow **[docs/back-end/code-quality.md](../../../docs/back-end/code-quality.md)** together with **[docs/back-end/architecture.md](../../../docs/back-end/architecture.md)**.

**SOLID (short)**

- **SRP:** one use case per class; thin controllers; split god services.
- **OCP:** extend via new **implementations** of ports, not giant conditionals.
- **LSP:** honour interface contracts in all implementations.
- **ISP:** small focused interfaces (`UserRepository`, `Clock`), not mega-ports.
- **DIP:** domain/application depend on **abstractions**; Eloquent and facades stay in **infrastructure** / delivery.

**Style**

- Run **Laravel Pint** before PR; **declare types** on public APIs; prefer **readonly** where values are immutable.
- Names reflect **ubiquitous language**, not generic `Manager`/`Helper`.

**Don’t**

- Import **Eloquent** or call **`DB::` / `Http::`** inside domain or use cases — use injected ports.
- Encode **domain invariants** only in FormRequests — critical rules belong on **entities/value objects**.

Reference: [docs/back-end/code-quality.md](../../../docs/back-end/code-quality.md)
